within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N01A_AnestheticsGeneral.N01AX10_Propofol;
model Propofol_Kim2023_PD_bis
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Kim_2023 :: BIS (bispectral index)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 92.1,      // [1]
    Emax = -18.7,  // [1]
    EC50 = 0.00221,  // [kg/m3; μg/mL × 0.001]
    gamma = 2.89,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 μg/mL per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 23, Interval = 0.046),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Propofol_Kim2023_PD_bis</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Kim KM et al., <i>Journal of pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics 50(2):97–109</i> 2023 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10928-022-09836-6\">doi:10.1007/s10928-022-09836-6</a>) — bispectral index against propofol μg/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       92.1          drug-free response (baseline) (E0, Q324)
  Emax  =       18.7          maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =       2.21 μg/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (Ce50, Q321)
  gamma =       2.89          Hill coefficient (γ, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one μg/mL of propofol per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 92.1   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (2.21 μg/mL)  response 82.75
  exposure -> infinity  response 73.4</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Kim_2023: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Propofol_Kim2023_PD_bis;
